<ProjectLayout
  title="Fives Machining"
  category="Experience | Machine Tools"
  year="Sept 2023 | Present"
  description="Progressive engineering experience at Fives Machining, from mechanical and hydraulic design to project management on large-scale 5-axis machine tools."
>

  <p slot="intro">
    A progressive engineering experience combining mechanical design,
    hydraulics, industrialisation and project management on large-scale
    5-axis machine tools.
  </p>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      01
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Evolution
      </h2>

      <p>
        I joined Fives Machining in September 2023 and progressively moved
        from mechanical and hydraulic design technician responsibilities
        toward engineering and project management.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Mechanical & Hydraulic Design Technician | Sept 2023 | Sept 2025
        </li>

        <li>
          Mechanical & Hydraulic Design Engineer | Sept 2025 | Sept 2026
        </li>

        <li>
          Project Manager Engineer | Sept 2026 | Present
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      02
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Machine tool engineering
      </h2>

      <p>
        My work has focused on the design and integration of mechanical assemblies
        for large-scale 5-axis milling machines.
      </p>

      <p>
        These machines can involve structures weighing up to 40 tons and require
        the integration of mechanical, hydraulic and industrial constraints within
        highly complex systems.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      03
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Hydraulic systems
      </h2>

      <p>
        I engineered hydraulic systems operating at pressures up to 300 bar,
        with particular attention to pressure stability and integration within
        the machine architecture.
      </p>

      <p>
        This work strengthened my understanding of hydraulic system design,
        component selection and industrial implementation.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      04
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Design optimisation
      </h2>

      <p>
        Standardisation of components contributed to reducing integration time
        by 65%.
      </p>

      <p>
        I also worked on improving maintenance accessibility, contributing to
        a reported 30% reduction in downtime.
      </p>

      <p>
        These activities reinforced the importance of considering assembly,
        maintenance and lifecycle constraints directly during the design phase.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


